<title>AUSTRALIA: Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index edges up.</title>
<headline>Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index edges up.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia said its index of commodity prices rose by 0.1 percent in Special Drawing Rights (SDR) terms in May after falling 1.0 percent in April.</p>
<p>Rises in the prices of wool, crude oil and base metals were partly offset by falls in the prices of beef and wheat, the central bank said.</p>
<p>In Australian dollar terms, the index rose by 1.4 percent after a fall of 0.3 percent in April.  </p>
<p>The Reserve Bank indices were as follows (base 1989/90):</p>
<p>		     All Items		    Rural Component</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	   A$	SDR	US$</p>
<p>May 97 p  94.2     88.7     94.9	 89.6     84.3     90.2</p>
<p>Apr 97 r  92.9     88.6     94.1	 89.1     84.9     90.2</p>
<p>May 96 r  95.3     88.3     98.7	 90.8     84.0     94.0</p>
<p>		 Non-Rural Component     of which: Base Metals</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	  A$	 SDR	US$</p>
<p>May 97 p  97.1     91.4     97.8	92.3	86.7     93.0</p>
<p>Apr 97 r  95.3     90.8     96.5	88.5	84.3     89.6</p>
<p>May 96 r  97.8     90.6    101.3	90.7	83.9     93.9</p>
<p>NOTE - r = revised, p = preliminary</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
